1
00:00:00,081 --> 00:00:01,441
Your chatbot answers.

2
00:00:01,915 --> 00:00:03,081
Why can't it act?

3
00:00:03,802 --> 00:00:05,268
If you are building AI

4
00:00:05,308 --> 00:00:07,657
projects, this difference decides what

5
00:00:07,698 --> 00:00:09,023
you actually build next.

6
00:00:09,764 --> 00:00:11,308
A chatbot is a software

7
00:00:11,368 --> 00:00:13,775
application that communicates with people

8
00:00:13,915 --> 00:00:15,239
through text or voice.

9
00:00:15,670 --> 00:00:16,892
Ask it when your exam

10
00:00:17,033 --> 00:00:18,616
is, and it answers, then

11
00:00:18,697 --> 00:00:20,000
waits for your next message.

12
00:00:20,390 --> 00:00:22,174
An agent is different: a

13
00:00:22,234 --> 00:00:24,780
system that autonomously performs tasks

14
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:27,045
by designing workflows with available

15
00:00:27,105 --> 00:00:27,446
tools.

16
00:00:27,796 --> 00:00:28,718
Give it a goal like

17
00:00:28,738 --> 00:00:30,921
"shortlist internships that match my

18
00:00:30,981 --> 00:00:32,724
résumé and add the deadlines

19
00:00:32,784 --> 00:00:34,067
to my calendar", and it

20
00:00:34,087 --> 00:00:36,390
plans the steps, searches, reads,

21
00:00:36,551 --> 00:00:38,354
shortlists and writes the entries

22
00:00:38,414 --> 00:00:38,814
itself.

23
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:41,712
Anthropic describes agents as systems

24
00:00:42,012 --> 00:00:43,276
where the model directs its

25
00:00:43,396 --> 00:00:44,980
own process and tool use.

26
00:00:45,741 --> 00:00:47,166
So here is the test.

27
00:00:47,557 --> 00:00:49,048
If it only talks, it

28
00:00:49,108 --> 00:00:49,874
is a chatbot.

29
00:00:50,225 --> 00:00:51,346
If it pursues a goal

30
00:00:51,586 --> 00:00:52,988
and completes tasks for you,

31
00:00:53,329 --> 00:00:54,250
it is an agent.

32
